Facts from other projects
-------------------------

Xiaomi does not document the miIO protocol, the MIoT requests or the Mi
account API. The facts this module uses were read from public
descriptions:

- python-miio (github.com/rytilahti/python-miio, GPL-3.0): the miIO
  packet, the token-derived key and IV, the hello handshake, the MIoT
  request shapes; from v0.2.0 also the legacy method names of Roborock
  vacuums, Yeelight and Philips lights, chuangmi plugs and zhimi
  purifiers, the lumi gateway sub-device methods and a few sub-device
  type numbers, the miIO.ota request and states, and the push scene
  (send_data_frame, miIO.xdel) layout; from v0.3.0 also the Roborock
  legacy method names and answer fields (consumables, cleaning history,
  do-not-disturb, timers, sound volume, custom mode, carpet mode), the
  mDNS instance name, miIO.config_router and the MIoT probe; its
  per-model fan speed tables were not taken. python-miio is GPL-licensed: no
  code was taken from it, and nothing in this module is a translation of
  it; only facts were used.
- Xiaomi-cloud-tokens-extractor
  (github.com/PiotrMachowski/Xiaomi-cloud-tokens-extractor; MIT,
  Copyright (c) 2020 Piotr Machowski): the Mi account sign-in steps, the
  RC4 and signature parameters, the API endpoints and the server
  regions; from v0.2.0 also the captcha and identity-check steps. No
  code was taken.
- Public descriptions of open-source Mi account clients: the
  device-control paths (miotspec/prop/get, miotspec/prop/set,
  miotspec/action, home/rpc). No code was taken.
- hass-xiaomi-miot (github.com/al-one/hass-xiaomi-miot, Apache-2.0,
  Copyright its authors), from v0.3.0: the full specification index, the
  translations path and the shape of their keys, the second host of the
  specification service. No code was taken.
- miot-spec.org: the format of MIoT specifications. No specification is
  bundled; HTTPSpecs fetches them at run time and SpecMirror keeps them
  in a directory the caller chooses.

The module contains no key, secret or credential of Xiaomi, of the
author or of any user. The Mi account client signs in with the
credentials its caller gives.

Interop tests (interop/, a separate test-only module)
-----------------------------------------------------

interop/peer/Dockerfile downloads python-miio (GPL-3.0) at a fixed
commit and installs it, with its dependencies, into a python:3.12.10-slim
image at test time, to run its device simulators and its packet code;
nothing of python-miio is copied into this repository, and it is not
linked with this module. interop/peer/spec.json is a made-up
specification of our own; interop/peer/push.py and interop/peer/spec.py
are our own scripts calling python-miio (and micloud, which it installs)
at test time. The Roborock simulator file the tests run is python-miio's
own, read inside the image; it is not copied here.

